<title>SOUTH KOREA: Tae Il gets $3.4 mln dividend from China venture.</title>
<headline>Tae Il gets $3.4 mln dividend from China venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Tae Il Media Co Ltd said on Monday it had received $3.4 million in dividends from its joint venture electronics firm in China.</p>
<p>A Tae Il statement said the dividend was a result of sales rises in the Chinese venture, Ssang Tae Electronics Industrial Group Co Ltd, where Tae Il holds an 80.8 percent stake.</p>
<p>Sales by Ssang Tae rose 74 percent to $131.3 million in 1996 from $88.17 million in 1995.</p>
<p>In 1996, Tae Il posted a 7.9 billion won net profit on sales of 390.5 billion won.</p>
</text>
